WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.825
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:12.095 --> 00:13.303
TOKYO

3
00:13.399 --> 00:16.909
Simultaneous kidnappings have struck seven cities in Asia!

4
00:18.290 --> 00:19.562
Not just Seoul.

5
00:20.159 --> 00:24.259
People were kidnapped in other Asian cities at the same time.

6
00:25.284 --> 00:28.623
In Singapore, a man was abducted in a restaurant.

7
00:29.576 --> 00:33.256
In Bangkok, a woman was apparently taken from her home.

8
00:34.041 --> 00:38.428
In Manila, a woman aged 20 was seized on her way home from work.

9
00:39.743 --> 00:44.201
In Taipei, a man was abducted in front of his teenage daughter.

10
00:45.659 --> 00:47.909
There was also a case in Naha.

11
00:53.409 --> 00:55.201
SAORI KIDNAP GAME

12
00:55.284 --> 00:57.284
"kiDnap GAME"?

13
00:57.618 --> 01:01.743
"Only one shall prevail... Only one shall survive..."

14
01:02.830 --> 01:04.580
MISSION

15
01:10.580 --> 01:13.039
CAPTURE THE MASTERMIND.

16
01:14.247 --> 01:17.080
Capture the mastermind...

17
02:01.580 --> 02:03.580
KIDNAP GAME

18
02:05.360 --> 02:08.902
39 HOURS UNTIL THE FIRST CASUALTY OF KIDNAP GAME

19
02:11.137 --> 02:14.220
SINGAPORE DAY 1

20
02:14.637 --> 02:17.553
Sir, I've just got this text!

21
02:17.637 --> 02:18.970
PM 07:00 SGT

22
02:19.877 --> 02:21.335
"kiDnap GAME?"

23
02:21.591 --> 02:24.209
It must be from the kidnapper. Tony was kidnapped.

24
02:25.303 --> 02:28.595
It says “Clear the checkpoints within the time limits and reach the goal.

25
02:28.720 --> 02:32.720
"Checkpoint One: The treasure-laden ship founders. Time limit: forty-four hours."

26
02:35.470 --> 02:39.137
Maybe you're famous enough to attract this kind of malicious prank.

27
02:39.762 --> 02:42.220
What do you mean? It’s not a prank!

28
02:42.345 --> 02:44.043
Tony will die if I don’t complete this mission.

29
02:44.095 --> 02:45.428
You’re already breaking this rule, though.

30
02:45.637 --> 02:49.220
It says “Do not notify or request assistance from state authorities,”

31
02:49.338 --> 02:50.490
but that’s us.

32
02:55.387 --> 02:56.350
Yeah.

33
02:59.159 --> 03:00.723
Yeah, it's a prank.

34
03:02.927 --> 03:05.650
You know, forget I mentioned it, it’s definitely a prank.

35
03:10.220 --> 03:13.845
TOKYO DAY 1

36
03:15.387 --> 03:19.012
PM 08:02 JST

37
03:24.220 --> 03:26.762
DO NOT NOTIFY OR REQUEST ASSISTANCE FROM STATE AUTHORITIES.

38
03:26.845 --> 03:28.303
RULE-BREAKERS WILL BE DISQUALIFIED.

39
03:29.928 --> 03:30.928
Niide? You okay?

40
03:31.512 --> 03:34.095
Yeah. Did you find anything out?

41
03:35.053 --> 03:39.012
We can't track the vehicle or locate her phone.

42
03:39.137 --> 03:42.803
What about witnesses?! There's got to be something!

43
03:42.887 --> 03:44.345
-But, um... -Move.

44
03:44.428 --> 03:45.595
Where are you going?

45
03:45.720 --> 03:49.262
Hold it, Niide! Think about what's happening.

46
03:50.320 --> 03:53.320
Simultaneous abductions in seven cities.

47
03:53.445 --> 03:55.362
We don't know their demands.

48
03:55.387 --> 03:56.670
They demand...

49
03:57.178 --> 03:59.512
“DO NOT NOTIFY OR REQUEST ASSISTANCE FROM STATE AUTHORITIES.

50
03:59.637 --> 04:01.928
RULE-BREAKERS WILL BE DISQUALIFIED.

51
04:03.095 --> 04:04.512
They demand...

52
04:09.678 --> 04:11.803
SHINJUKU CENTRAL POLICE STATION

53
04:11.887 --> 04:13.262
AM 09:12 JST

54
04:13.345 --> 04:14.512
NOTICE OF LEAVE

55
04:15.922 --> 04:17.381
What the hell is this?

56
04:18.063 --> 04:19.480
You need to stay home.

57
04:19.563 --> 04:21.563
What's the meaning of this?

58
04:24.688 --> 04:26.480
KIDNAPPING VICTIMS NAMED

59
04:26.563 --> 04:28.476
SAORI NIIDE TOMIKO HIGA

60
04:28.563 --> 04:33.230
Why is Saori's name in the news? Someone here is leaking info!

61
04:33.313 --> 04:34.896
That's not possible...

62
04:35.473 --> 04:36.772
I can't trust anyone.

63
04:37.998 --> 04:40.235
I'll save her myself.

64
04:40.681 --> 04:44.181
What can you do alone? The SIT suspects you!

65
04:44.264 --> 04:46.181
They're way off mark!

66
04:46.264 --> 04:48.598
Expect to be watched.

67
04:48.880 --> 04:52.050
We can't help you either. You've got no allies.

68
04:53.829 --> 04:55.023
I know.

69
04:59.786 --> 05:01.453
Where are you going?

70
05:01.538 --> 05:03.496
This is a grudge against me.

71
05:03.580 --> 05:05.455
Have you got a lead?!

72
05:05.505 --> 05:06.850
Out of the way!

73
05:06.968 --> 05:09.593
We received a tip regarding Saori!

74
05:12.880 --> 05:16.710
A food vendor at the hospital kept seeing a suspicious van.

75
05:17.569 --> 05:18.536
A suspicious van?

76
05:20.295 --> 05:21.462
Here.

77
05:21.706 --> 05:23.248
FLORIST'S VAN, ROSE LOGO HOSPITAL

78
05:23.508 --> 05:24.633
Thanks.

79
05:27.547 --> 05:29.119
-That's him. -Let's go.

80
05:29.300 --> 05:30.193
Heading out.

81
05:46.630 --> 05:49.903
Sorry! I'll be open in about ten minutes.

82
05:50.588 --> 05:53.256
I'm Niide, from Shinjuku Central Police.

83
05:55.297 --> 05:56.243
Are you Saori's...?

84
05:56.922 --> 05:57.880
Yes.

85
05:59.172 --> 06:03.172
I heard you saw a suspicious florist's van.

86
06:03.730 --> 06:04.422
Yes.

87
06:06.630 --> 06:10.463
It parked over there every day for about a week.

88
06:11.005 --> 06:12.523
It was there yesterday, too.

89
06:13.380 --> 06:14.255
And the driver?

90
06:15.172 --> 06:16.755
I couldn't see inside.

91
06:17.338 --> 06:19.172
Anything else suspicious?

92
06:20.088 --> 06:21.123
Not particularly.

93
06:22.380 --> 06:23.063
I see.

94
06:29.838 --> 06:33.005
Do you not like carrots, by any chance?

95
06:33.630 --> 06:35.505
No.

96
06:35.563 --> 06:40.271
Saori asked me about carrot recipes more than once.

97
06:41.505 --> 06:44.338
I figured it was for someone special.

98
06:46.899 --> 06:47.556
Um...

99
06:48.630 --> 06:51.922
This is my phone number.

100
06:52.713 --> 06:56.350
Please call me if you remember anything else.

101
06:57.005 --> 06:58.047
Okay.

102
07:31.838 --> 07:32.672
How is it?

103
07:33.505 --> 07:35.755
Delicious.

104
07:36.797 --> 07:39.088
Eat a lot. It'll cure your temper.

105
07:40.255 --> 07:44.213
Beta-carotene doesn't have that effect, does it?

106
07:46.130 --> 07:49.963
It does if you think so. Trust me, I'm a nurse.

107
07:51.213 --> 07:52.255
I trust you.

108
07:53.172 --> 07:54.213
Seconds, then?

109
07:54.797 --> 07:57.505
-What?! Wait... -No ifs, no buts.

110
08:14.683 --> 08:18.433
How do you know the missing nurse?

111
08:20.572 --> 08:23.896
I met her when I was hospitalized and became friends.

112
08:26.503 --> 08:28.884
So you can talk to her husband...

113
08:29.883 --> 08:32.876
I can't push an interview on him now.

114
08:34.756 --> 08:37.169
This is a chance to redeem yourself.

115
08:43.338 --> 08:44.255
Excuse me.

116
08:46.078 --> 08:47.286
Hello?

117
08:48.187 --> 08:49.853
I need a favor.

118
08:51.230 --> 08:53.522
Get me info on the other hostages.

119
08:53.963 --> 08:55.297
Why me?

120
08:55.380 --> 08:58.838
I can't rely on the police. I'm a suspect.

121
09:00.917 --> 09:03.917
A regular investigation won't cut it.

122
09:04.251 --> 09:08.792
I need a different approach. And I need your help for that.

123
09:11.088 --> 09:11.963
All right.

124
09:12.630 --> 09:13.880
Thanks.

125
09:23.047 --> 09:24.213
Crap.

126
09:38.005 --> 09:40.047
-Where is he? -He got away.

127
09:40.172 --> 09:41.463
Dammit.

128
09:43.005 --> 09:45.297
These are the other hostages.

129
09:45.838 --> 09:47.255
Thanks.

130
09:48.063 --> 09:50.147
With this doctor's daughter,

131
09:50.254 --> 09:54.504
and this IT CEO's mother, the motive could be ransom.

132
09:55.297 --> 09:59.047
The man in Taipei is married to a famous model.

133
09:59.720 --> 10:02.136
The Bangkok woman's family is rich.

134
10:04.236 --> 10:08.270
But this girl in Manila comes from a poor family,

135
10:09.115 --> 10:13.865
and her grandfather even had to work in Japan as a delivery driver.

136
10:16.310 --> 10:19.922
If the objective isn't money, what could it be...?

137
10:20.935 --> 10:24.310
Some kind of revenge, or grudge...

138
10:25.366 --> 10:28.075
Who could hold a grudge against Saori?

139
10:29.098 --> 10:33.890
The grudge is probably against me. Saori's just caught up in this.

140
10:35.705 --> 10:37.330
If that's the case,

141
10:38.080 --> 10:41.372
could the same person resent these people, too?

142
10:42.225 --> 10:43.142
No way.

143
10:44.370 --> 10:45.537
I guess not.

144
10:45.562 --> 10:51.310
If it's not about money or revenge, and the victims were chosen at random...

145
10:52.919 --> 10:56.503
Is it just to make headlines or for the fun of it?

146
11:00.271 --> 11:01.896
Did you think of something?

147
11:03.255 --> 11:04.547
No...

148
11:07.763 --> 11:12.047
If the criminal's a thrill-seeker who wants to make headlines,

149
11:12.130 --> 11:14.243
you won't be able to stop him alone.

150
11:15.083 --> 11:18.005
I'm gonna hunt the bastard down.

151
11:19.032 --> 11:21.763
That attitude is what pained Saori.

152
11:21.794 --> 11:23.163
Then what am I supposed to do?

153
11:24.390 --> 11:26.383
You need to stay level-headed.

154
11:31.015 --> 11:32.136
What do you plan to do?

155
11:35.349 --> 11:38.230
I met a strange man the night before last.

156
11:39.640 --> 11:41.936
I'll investigate him.

157
11:43.664 --> 11:47.085
PM 05:03 JST

158
11:52.920 --> 11:54.253
Akina?

159
11:54.337 --> 11:57.712
Hey, you know anything about the "kiDnap GAME"?

160
12:00.710 --> 12:04.550
The girlfriend of the victim in Singapore is an influencer,

161
12:05.376 --> 12:08.710
and she made a post about this "kiDnap GAME" thing.

162
12:09.002 --> 12:11.002
It's kinda gone viral.

163
12:11.251 --> 12:15.543
ANYONE HEARD OF THE KIDNAP GAME?

164
12:19.803 --> 12:22.469
-Sorry. -It's okay.

165
12:29.835 --> 12:32.710
Oh, no. Oh no, wait, wait...

166
12:33.751 --> 12:35.168
You never heard of it?

167
12:37.626 --> 12:40.626
Never.

168
12:41.085 --> 12:42.251
Oh well.

169
12:42.918 --> 12:46.751
I thought it was worth mentioning. I'll keep digging.

170
12:46.918 --> 12:48.960
Okay, thanks.

171
12:56.157 --> 12:59.616
PM 09:45 JST

172
13:24.772 --> 13:25.897
Toyoda.

173
13:26.334 --> 13:27.251
Niide?

174
13:27.335 --> 13:29.169
I need to see some footage.

175
13:30.178 --> 13:34.282
Is this about your wife's case? I can't authorize that.

176
13:34.491 --> 13:36.032
Her trail's gone cold.

177
13:36.116 --> 13:37.616
It's a different person.

178
13:38.574 --> 13:42.491
Please. Saori's life depends on it.

179
13:48.116 --> 13:51.449
My shift ends in ten minutes. We need to hurry.

180
13:51.532 --> 13:52.407
Thanks.

181
13:54.077 --> 13:59.202
Tokyo Metro Tocho Nishimae Station, night before last, 11 PM.

182
14:26.366 --> 14:27.616
That's him.

183
14:27.907 --> 14:30.449
I'll track him with face recognition.

184
14:52.592 --> 14:55.336
That's the place? Thanks.

185
14:56.616 --> 14:59.782
PM 11:54 JST

186
17:08.616 --> 17:11.199
Saori! Saori!

187
17:16.491 --> 17:23.290
I'M NOT THE ONE YOU'RE AFTER! THE GAME GOES ON!

188
17:38.393 --> 17:39.496
Dammit!

189
17:54.394 --> 17:57.935
"BAR NEON LIGHT," KABUKICHO, NOON TOMORROW.

190
18:18.851 --> 18:21.309
Why are you doing this?

191
18:25.309 --> 18:28.810
My husband is a detective. He'll come for me, just you wait.

192
18:30.892 --> 18:32.767
He'll come for me!

193
18:36.226 --> 18:38.809
SEOUL DAY 1

194
18:38.892 --> 18:40.559
PM 08:00 KST

195
18:44.767 --> 18:47.434
MISSION

196
18:55.184 --> 18:56.351
Kiju?!

197
18:59.267 --> 18:59.976
Ayun.

198
19:00.001 --> 19:03.250
Where's Rian? Where?

199
19:03.931 --> 19:09.596
It's my fault. I took my eyes off her.

200
19:11.570 --> 19:14.029
Why would you do that?!

201
19:14.615 --> 19:17.574
Rian can't see anything!

202
19:29.101 --> 19:32.642
AM 10:12 KST

203
19:47.226 --> 19:51.601
KO WOON-MUK

204
20:24.476 --> 20:26.892
THIS COMPLETES MY MISSION, DOES IT NOT?

205
20:36.559 --> 20:40.017
GAME RULES VIOLATED. YOU ARE DISQUALIFIED.

206
20:43.892 --> 20:46.559
No, no, no!

207
20:48.684 --> 20:51.934
I APOLOGIZE. PLEASE DON’T HURT RIAN.

208
21:16.434 --> 21:20.193
ONE MORE FALSE REPORT AND YOUR DAUGHTER DIES.

209
21:32.359 --> 21:34.025
Are you okay, Dr. Han?

210
21:43.260 --> 21:46.874
My deepest sympathies. Is there any way I can help?

211
21:51.547 --> 21:52.810
Will you be needing a body?

212
21:57.553 --> 21:58.489
What do you mean?

213
21:59.516 --> 22:01.950
I can take care of unsavory work.

214
22:09.018 --> 22:13.518
It was you, was it? Where were you last night?

215
22:14.437 --> 22:16.490
Did you send me that bogus text?

216
22:18.576 --> 22:21.226
People are watching, Doctor.

217
22:53.857 --> 22:56.107
MISSION

218
22:56.232 --> 23:00.107
COMMIT MURDER.

219
23:08.288 --> 23:11.690
PM 02:22 KST

220
23:12.899 --> 23:14.524
But it's too far.

221
23:14.607 --> 23:16.565
It's possible.

222
23:42.815 --> 23:45.440
MISSION COMMIT MURDER.

223
23:50.788 --> 23:51.830
Where were you?

224
24:05.940 --> 24:07.982
Why Rian?

225
24:10.897 --> 24:13.553
She's not someone people would resent...

226
24:15.390 --> 24:20.643
If anyone's resented, it's us. We're living in too much luxury...

227
24:21.722 --> 24:26.819
We're hated and resented!

228
24:29.386 --> 24:30.423
Maybe.

229
24:34.783 --> 24:40.556
Get her back! I don't care about this lifestyle...

230
24:42.806 --> 24:44.950
I only need Rian!

231
24:48.211 --> 24:49.086
Come here.

232
24:52.743 --> 24:54.429
I feel the same way.

233
24:56.989 --> 24:58.909
Do you really?

234
25:00.266 --> 25:02.795
Five years ago, you could have saved her.

235
25:05.625 --> 25:07.667
You took the light from her.

236
25:17.257 --> 25:19.465
PM 11:45 KST

237
25:19.632 --> 25:24.632
INTENSIVE CARE UNIT

238
25:58.424 --> 26:01.174
COMMIT MURDER.

239
26:05.632 --> 26:07.299
Kill me...

240
26:09.507 --> 26:14.590
Put me out of my misery...

241
26:25.843 --> 26:27.218
Dr. Han?

242
26:29.007 --> 26:29.976
Looking for something?

243
26:30.602 --> 26:34.116
No, it's fine.

244
26:36.795 --> 26:37.736
Dr. Han.

245
26:40.523 --> 26:44.843
Were you asking today about where Mr. Park, the undertaker,

246
26:45.117 --> 26:47.696
was last night?

247
26:50.070 --> 26:54.576
He was at the hospital shortly before you phoned us.

248
26:55.612 --> 26:58.170
I was wondering what he was doing...

249
27:03.653 --> 27:10.076
Someone help me... Dad... Mom...

250
27:14.416 --> 27:18.862
MANILA DAY 1

251
27:26.817 --> 27:31.217
It’s your birthday soon, right Lolo? Anything you want?

252
27:32.403 --> 27:36.987
No it's okay. Don’t worry, I’ve been saving up money just like you...

253
27:37.112 --> 27:39.945
Yeah. So what do you want?

254
27:40.070 --> 27:43.243
Clothes? Shoes? Or...

255
27:43.742 --> 27:44.781
No! No!

256
27:45.029 --> 27:48.237
Maria! Maria, what’s happening?!

257
27:54.153 --> 27:56.195
MISSION

258
27:56.320 --> 27:59.903
PREPARE 10 MILLION PESOS IN CASH.

259
28:05.445 --> 28:06.612
Maria...

260
28:09.987 --> 28:13.445
AM 07:22 PHT

261
28:18.778 --> 28:20.445
I'm back!

262
28:21.096 --> 28:22.376
Maria!

263
28:23.987 --> 28:27.653
Here, pocket money.

264
28:28.482 --> 28:30.857
All this? Are you sure?

265
28:32.161 --> 28:35.453
Dad, you shouldn’t give her money every time just like that.

266
28:35.945 --> 28:39.362
I got a big tip from a rich tourist today.

267
28:39.487 --> 28:44.503
It’s because you’re the best! Thank you!

268
28:56.945 --> 29:01.903
Dad, You conned that money from those tourists, didn’t you?

269
29:05.112 --> 29:10.528
You’ve got to stop that, Dad. Life isn’t all about money.

270
29:12.533 --> 29:16.366
You only say that because you haven't been poor.

271
29:19.278 --> 29:23.487
People who chase money get what’s coming to them.

272
29:27.403 --> 29:29.278
Nothing comes.

273
29:30.869 --> 29:34.849
There’s no God, no Buddha to punish anyone.

274
29:36.196 --> 29:39.779
I’m done with the shame of begging,

275
29:41.136 --> 29:44.695
done with being worked to the bone in a foreign country.

276
29:45.820 --> 29:49.945
You think I can let my daughter and granddaughter go through that?!

277
30:05.076 --> 30:07.451
Please! Sir! Wait!

278
30:07.493 --> 30:11.922
Miguel, you’re a great employee and a great friend, but you’ll make a terrible debtor.

279
30:13.149 --> 30:16.636
-Why? -You’re too old to pay it back.

280
30:17.416 --> 30:21.749
But sir, I’ll do anything! I'll work day and night for the rest of my life...

281
30:21.810 --> 30:25.596
That’s how accidents happen. I won’t let you do that.

282
30:26.845 --> 30:28.143
That’s all I have to say.

283
31:15.737 --> 31:17.278
Hi, sir. Good morning.

284
31:22.461 --> 31:23.689
Cash me in.

285
31:29.335 --> 31:30.699
All in on 12.

286
31:32.403 --> 31:33.778
Are you sure, sir?

287
31:36.320 --> 31:37.320
Yes.

288
32:16.132 --> 32:18.299
Wait, wait! One more time.

289
32:18.632 --> 32:21.965
One more time. Please, give me another chance!

290
32:22.090 --> 32:25.143
-Excuse me, sir. Was there a problem here? -One more time!

291
32:25.174 --> 32:28.176
-Sorry, you have to go! -Please! Maria’s life depends on it!

292
32:28.216 --> 32:33.091
Please! Maria’s life depends on it! Wait! No, no, no...

293
32:33.780 --> 32:36.853
Please wait! Give me one more chance!

294
32:40.006 --> 32:40.860
Please don't come back!

295
32:42.905 --> 32:44.956
-Please! -Stop it!

296
32:52.340 --> 32:53.516
“kiDnap GAME”?

297
32:54.856 --> 32:55.924
This.

298
32:59.003 --> 33:01.048
Could be a prank, but if not...

299
33:02.170 --> 33:04.063
“Only one shall survive”!

300
33:06.183 --> 33:09.730
If we do not collect the ten million pesos before the others,

301
33:11.458 --> 33:14.169
then Maria gets killed! Do you get that?!

302
33:17.389 --> 33:19.463
We need to get the money right away!

303
33:24.892 --> 33:26.267
I know where to get the money.

304
33:27.992 --> 33:29.158
Where?

305
33:32.132 --> 33:33.715
The bank.

306
33:35.590 --> 33:36.507
What?

307
33:37.965 --> 33:40.382
We'll get the money from the bank I work at.

308
33:41.911 --> 33:44.286
I know how the bank operates.

309
33:45.816 --> 33:48.715
Most bank robberies fail. How can this work?

310
33:49.007 --> 33:53.049
We just need to hand over the money, right?

311
33:56.378 --> 33:57.596
I get it.

312
33:59.465 --> 34:01.757
I don’t care if I get caught.

313
34:03.345 --> 34:07.386
As long as we get the money, we can save Maria!

314
34:07.507 --> 34:11.299
Right. we're fine even if you get caught.

315
34:11.762 --> 34:13.736
It doesn't matter if I get caught.

316
34:16.924 --> 34:18.924
I don't care if I die.

317
34:20.621 --> 34:23.204
As long as Maria’s safe!

318
34:29.715 --> 34:36.196
Help me. Please save me. Please let me out. I'm begging you. Please help!

319
34:43.608 --> 34:46.692
KIDNAP GAME DAY 2

320
34:48.257 --> 34:51.465
AM 07:49 PHT

321
34:54.295 --> 34:57.154
Good morning, sir.

322
34:58.996 --> 35:03.090
-I’m very sorry about yesterday. -That’s fine, forget it.

323
35:04.330 --> 35:07.965
Oh, you’ve got a flat tire.

324
35:08.470 --> 35:10.965
Right before an important meeting.

325
35:12.421 --> 35:16.229
I can take you, if you like. By way of apology.

326
35:16.696 --> 35:17.882
That would be good.

327
35:35.913 --> 35:37.246
I hope you didn’t kill him.

328
35:37.724 --> 35:39.724
He’s fine. More importantly...

329
36:10.688 --> 36:16.041
I would like to deposit a company deed. I’m acting as an agent.

330
36:16.965 --> 36:18.132
Ma'am.

331
36:24.007 --> 36:26.215
ENTRANCE

332
36:34.618 --> 36:38.650
-Hey Ricky. Cash truck is arriving. -OK.

333
36:49.036 --> 36:54.883
May I see some kind of IDs to confirm your and the principal’s names and addresses?

334
37:02.037 --> 37:03.117
Oh, thank you.

335
37:14.806 --> 37:15.973
Thank you.

336
37:32.240 --> 37:33.698
Sorry for keeping you waiting, sir.

337
37:34.547 --> 37:35.520
This way, please.

338
37:44.182 --> 37:47.890
KABUKICHO FIRST AVENUE

339
38:03.062 --> 38:04.645
Welcome.

340
38:11.105 --> 38:12.397
You made it.

341
38:13.118 --> 38:17.490
The fact that you're here means that you destroyed our dummy.

342
38:18.089 --> 38:19.464
So predictable.

343
38:19.781 --> 38:22.740
Don't touch me if you care about your wife.

344
38:22.906 --> 38:24.240
Where is she?!

345
38:27.179 --> 38:28.679
On the track.

346
38:30.198 --> 38:31.303
Did you text me?

347
38:31.883 --> 38:34.196
You mean about the game?

348
38:35.823 --> 38:39.406
I'm not playing around. People could die.

349
38:40.740 --> 38:46.115
-May I help you carry your bag, sir? -No no, it's OK.

350
38:55.490 --> 38:58.115
-You may come in, sir. -Thank you.

351
39:05.865 --> 39:11.031
Oh, sorry. I left my key at the desk.

352
39:11.323 --> 39:14.365
No problem, sir. I'll just get it for you.

353
39:15.165 --> 39:15.998
Thank you.

354
39:48.193 --> 39:49.109
Are you okay, sir?

355
39:52.615 --> 39:54.740
Hey! Stop! Come back!

356
39:54.865 --> 39:58.448
Emergency! The guard took a case of money!

357
40:00.573 --> 40:01.823
He’s on the run! Stop him!

358
40:12.615 --> 40:13.531
Stop!

359
40:18.281 --> 40:22.740
Stop! Freeze!

360
40:23.365 --> 40:24.490
Stop!

361
40:28.173 --> 40:32.983
No! Please no! I need that money. My daughter’s been kidnapped. Please!

362
40:33.573 --> 40:35.240
I'll tell you something.

363
40:36.003 --> 40:39.365
One player's almost completed his mission.

364
40:42.084 --> 40:45.736
He's risking everything to raise a king's ransom.

365
40:48.490 --> 40:52.115
The man in Manila? That's his mission?

366
40:52.948 --> 40:54.448
So whatcha gonna do?

367
40:57.281 --> 40:59.031
There's nothing you can do.

368
41:18.740 --> 41:20.115
What's going on?

369
41:23.448 --> 41:25.115
Where is the money, Ricky?

370
41:28.948 --> 41:30.031
No way...

371
41:53.823 --> 41:55.156
Excuse me, sir.

372
42:56.323 --> 42:59.589
Throw away your guns! Throw away your guns!

373
43:02.653 --> 43:04.695
You! You!

374
43:06.490 --> 43:11.436
Put the money... all the money! All the money, now!

375
43:16.103 --> 43:18.615
Give it to me! Give it to me!

376
43:52.548 --> 43:55.588
Stop the car!

377
43:56.108 --> 43:58.728
Get out of the car!

378
44:15.443 --> 44:20.781
Get out of the car! Now! Hands up!

379
44:38.550 --> 44:39.876
Oh, God no!

380
44:41.992 --> 44:44.200
Please.

381
44:50.676 --> 44:54.906
Maria, Maria...

382
44:58.516 --> 45:02.423
Maria, Maria...!

383
45:35.563 --> 45:37.636
Read it. I'm not going to run.

384
45:52.592 --> 45:54.092
It's a game!

385
45:54.448 --> 45:58.686
It's a game! Maria's going to die. Please!

386
46:01.208 --> 46:05.182
We're not playing around. People could die.

387
46:08.198 --> 46:11.281
PLAYERS DEEMED INCAPABLE OF COMPLETING THEIR MISSION WILL BE IMMEDIATELY DISQUALIFIED.

388
47:21.176 --> 47:22.259
Mama?

389
47:23.563 --> 47:24.636
Are you okay?

390
47:27.771 --> 47:28.249
Yeah...

391
47:50.146 --> 47:54.438
Hey, you haven't told anyone about us, have you?

392
48:10.077 --> 48:11.286
Is it real?

393
48:12.936 --> 48:14.450
It’s actually for real...?

394
48:16.359 --> 48:19.389
Oh no... I’m running out of time...

395
48:20.462 --> 48:22.379
“The treasure-laden ship founders”?

396
48:23.188 --> 48:25.271
What’s that meant to mean?!

397
48:32.438 --> 48:35.730
TANG SHIPWRECK

398
48:35.855 --> 48:38.480
CHINESE TREASURES FROM THE 9TH CENTURY...

399
48:39.188 --> 48:41.980
This must be it!

400
48:44.771 --> 48:46.230
Why?

401
48:50.855 --> 48:53.313
Why are you doing this to us?

402
49:13.368 --> 49:16.063
KIDNAP GAME CO-PRODUCTION PARTNERSHIP

403
49:16.146 --> 49:17.521
FUJI TELEVISION MAKERVILLE SIMSTORY

404
49:17.646 --> 49:21.648
BASED ON KIDNAP GAME CREATED BY YUSUKE KATO
